[2026-09-04T15:53:39.653Z] [802347e2-49c3-4767-8f61-de8f9dbc818a] INFO REVIEW COMPLETE | iteration=1 | score=84 | rootCause=The render is visually appetizing and the hook works, but the actual execution does not match the intended premium commercial finish: the reel is effectively an 11-shot-ish montage compressed into 13.5s with repeated static holds, weak/unfinished typography, minimal audible finish, and no real brand presence beyond generic CTA text. The biggest problem is that the middle and end feel like raw footage with overlaid words rather than a polished, intentional commercial cut. | issues=[{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Typography","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The hook text 'Fresh.' is simple, but the overall text system in the render looks generic and not fully premium; later CTA text is large, centered, and feels like a template overlay rather than custom commercial design.","fix":"Use one refined hook word only, then a cleaner premium CTA treatment with smaller type, better spacing, safer lower-third/center balance, and stronger brand styling consistency."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Pacing","timestamp_seconds":4.5,"problem":"The reel lingers too long on nearly identical plating frames (multiple static repeats around the three-plate overhead), creating visible dead time instead of momentum.","fix":"Trim the reveal to a single clean beat or a very short two-shot sequence; cut away faster once the arrangement is readable."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Continuity","timestamp_seconds":10.5,"problem":"The ending feels like a hold on the same hero setup for too many frames, making the CTA section repetitive rather than purposeful.","fix":"Use one decisive CTA hold, not a prolonged loop; land the text earlier and let the final frame breathe without repeated near-identical duplication."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Brand","timestamp_seconds":11,"problem":"There is no real brand identity beyond the words 'KAIRO Sushi'; no logo lockup, signage, or branded finish is visible, so the ad feels generic.","fix":"If no brand assets exist in footage, make the CTA layout feel like a deliberate end card through typography, spacing, and a consistent branded color treatment."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Audio","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The render does not feel like a finished commercial sonically; the brief calls for a premium audio bed with SFX punctuation, but the execution appears sparse and not fully realized.","fix":"Strengthen the sound design: torch sizzle, plate set, knife click/crunch, and a more confident CTA hit, with a polished music bed underneath."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Visual Variety","timestamp_seconds":4,"problem":"Several frames recycle the same visual idea—hands plating on a white surface—without enough change in angle or action to keep the montage feeling dynamic.","fix":"Intercut the craft shots more aggressively and reduce any repeated static presentation before the bite reaction."}]
